{"Title":"An Act relative to Yarmouth tourism funding change","BillNumber":"H3796","DocketNumber":"HD2284","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"CRF1","Name":"Christopher Richard Flanagan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CRF1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T12:06:56.11"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"CRF1","Name":"Christopher Richard Flanagan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CRF1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T12:06:56.11"},{"Id":"KAD1","Name":"Kip A. Diggs","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/KAD1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T12:06:56.25"},{"Id":"CAD1","Name":"Carol A. Doherty","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CAD1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-07T09:20:51.57"},{"Id":"JAC0","Name":"Julian Cyr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JAC0","ResponseDate":"2023-02-08T17:14:45.4433333"}],"JointSponsor":{"Id":"JAC0","Name":"Julian Cyr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JAC0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T12:06:56.11"},"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3796/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Flanagan of Dennis and Senator Cyr, a joint petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3796) of Christopher Richard Flanagan, Julian Cyr and others (by vote of the town) relative to authorizing the town of Yarmouth to establish a tourism revenue preservation fund.  Revenue.  [Local Approval Received.]","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Chapter 338 of the acts of 2006 is hereby amended by striking out section 1 and inserting in place thereof the following section:-\r\n\tSECTION 1. Notwithstanding section 53 of chapter 44 of the General Laws or any other general or special law to the contrary, the town of Yarmouth shall establish in the town treasury a special account to be known as the Tourism Revenue Preservation Fund of the town of Yarmouth, into which account shall be deposited certain receipts comprising a portion of the total local room occupancy tax, excepting taxes generated by short term rentals, received annually by the town under section 3A of chapter 64G of the General Laws, as set forth in section 2, as well as any grants, gifts or donations made to the town in furtherance of the purposes of this act.\r\n\tSECTION 2. This act shall take effect upon its passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H52","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H52"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Correctly Drawn","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H36","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H36"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}